# LexDroid configuration. Copy to .env and fill in what you need.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored. Nothing here is required to run the core pipeline: Engine A is local and
# needs no key, which is the Section 3 claim -- the tool runs end to end with no proprietary API.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Engine B, on a rented GPU.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# qwen3.8-lex-16k runs on a RunPod GPU the interface rents for it (Start a run -> Runs on ->
# Rent GPU). That needs a RunPod API key; leave it empty and the interface still offers Engine A,
# which answers everything on its own. Either line works; RUNPOD_API_KEY in the environment wins.
#
# The key stays on this machine: it is never sent to the pod or written anywhere else.
# api=
# RUNPOD_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A hosted engine, if one is ever declared. Optional.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# An engine in backend/data/engines.json marked hosted reads its key from here. None is declared
# now. The host and model are never set here; a key in that file would be a key in a backup.
LEXDROID_HOSTED_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local engine hosts. Optional.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where Ollama is. Defaults to http://127.0.0.1:11434.
# OLLAMA_HOST=http://127.0.0.1:11434
#
# Several endpoints for a fleet, comma-separated. The fleet refuses a host listed twice.
# OLLAMA_HOSTS=http://127.0.0.1:11701,http://127.0.0.1:11702
#
# A bearer token, if a host sits behind a token-checking proxy. Never written to a file by the tool.
# LEXDROID_ENGINE_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Models. Optional -- the defaults are what is declared.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LEXDROID_READING_MODEL=gemma4-lex-16k
# LEXDROID_EMBEDDING_MODEL=bge-m3

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The engine cache. Off unless set, and it must stay off for any quotable run.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Replays stored engine answers instead of asking for them. Turns a forty-minute pillar into
# seconds while a scoring rule is being worked on -- and turns a measurement into a replay. A run
# that used it carries a note on its own record saying it is not quotable.
# LEXDROID_ENGINE_CACHE=1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read-only hosted snapshot. Optional; Vercel enables this automatically.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Use this on another serverless host to disable pipeline and review writes while serving the
# checked-in analysis snapshot.
# LEXDROID_READ_ONLY=1
